<!--
    Device framework compatibility matrix.

    The stock per-HAL VINTF fragments we ship declare 45 vendor-specific AIDL
    instances (vendor.qti.*, vendor.zte.*). None of them exist in any AOSP
    framework compatibility matrix, so check_vintf_all fails the build with
      ERROR: files are incompatible: The following instances are in the device
      manifest but not specified in framework compatibility matrix
    checkvintf itself names the fix: declare device-specific HALs in
    DEVICE_FRAMEWORK_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX_FILE.

    Every entry is optional="true". These are vendor HALs: the framework must
    tolerate their absence, not require them. Marking any of them required would
    turn a missing vendor service into a boot failure.

    Generated from the checkvintf error output, not hand-written - the package,
    interface, instance and version of each entry are exactly what the device
    manifest declares.
-->
